      "narrative": null,
      "content": "KEROV’S CENTRAL LIMIT THEOREM FOR SCHUR-WEYL\nMEASURES OF PARAMETER α = 1/2\nPIERRE-LOÏC MÉLIOT\nAbstract. In this article, we show that Kerov’s central limit theorem related to the ﬂuctuations of\nYoung diagrams under the Plancherel measure extends to the case of Schur-Weyl measures, which are\nthe probability measures on partitions associated to the representations of the symmetric groups Sn on\ntensor products of vector spaces V ⊗n (see [Bia01]). The proof is inspired by the one given in [IO02] for\nthe Plancherel measure, and it relies on the combinatorics of the algebra of observables of diagram",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
