      "target": "../sections/sec-000-1-schur-weyl-measures-of-parameter-12.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "[]{#swbiane label=\"swbiane\"} In the following, we fix two positive real numbers $\\alpha$ and $c$. Recall that the irreducible representations of the symmetric group $\\sym_{n}$ are labelled by partitions of size $n$, that is to say, non-increasing sequences $$\\lambda=(\\lambda_{1},\\ldots,\\lambda_{r})$$ of positive integers that sum up to $n$; see for instance [@Weyl39 Chapter 4]. Such a sequence can be represented by its **Young diagram**, which is an array of $n$ boxes with $\\lambda_{1}$ boxes in the first line, $\\lambda_{2}$ boxes in the second line, etc.\n\nWe denote by $\\Part_{n}$ the set of i",
